, \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1794255906559413001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"49529de1-03a4-4a3e-9053-9bb22c796c7f","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"75af-1212-aa22-463f"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nA non-blocking PASS under either engine must earn the same certification: a signed plan-review attestation the claim gate, the close gate, `review-plan --status` and `sign-review` accept (ADR 0049, `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py`). For the two engines to be auditable side by side, the attestation must also record which engine produced it.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd an `engine` field (`\"pipeline\"` or `\"agentic\"`) to the signed payload that `attest.sign_plan_review` (`attest.py:113`) builds, taken from the verdict's coverage the adapter sets. The field sits inside the signed bytes, so it cannot be edited without breaking the signature. Readers treat a missing field as `\"pipeline\"`, so every attestation signed before this change keeps validating for claim, close, `--status` and `sign-review`; no migration is written. `resign.py` (re-signing) carries the field forward unchanged. `review-plan --status` and the MCP `plan_review_status` output show the engine. Putting provenance on the attestation itself, rather than only on the sidecar, is what makes it survive sidecar pruning (`sidecar.prune`).\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py (payload field, reader default)\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/resign.py (carry forward)\n- src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json (engine field)\n- the `review-plan --status` renderer and `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py` status output\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_engine.py (new)\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: an agentic PASS signs an attestation with `engine: \"agentic\"`; the claim gate accepts it, `review-plan --status` reports it current, and `sign-review` re-certifies it with the field intact.\n- Back-compat: a fixture attestation without the field validates and reads as `\"pipeline\"`.\n- Tamper: editing `engine` in a signed attestation fails signature verification.\n- Refusal: an agentic INDETERMINATE or BLOCK is not signed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Agentic PASS attestations record `engine: \"agentic\"` and are accepted by claim, close, `review-plan --status` and `sign-review`, pinned by `tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_engine.py`.\n- [ ] Pre-existing attestations without the field keep validating, pinned by the back-compat test.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py","reason":"engine field"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/resign.py","reason":"carry forward"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json","reason":"engine in status"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py","reason":"status output"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review_attest_engine.py","reason":"new tests"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","75af-1212-aa22-463f"],["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"4cc4-3b8b-e554-41ef","ticket_type":"story","title":"Record the plan-review engine on the signed attestation","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["cce97a68-cfd3-4785-bd3f-2956ac853067","49529de1-03a4-4a3e-9053-9bb22c796c7f","98f757c0-2077-4f63-98f2-927079576160"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794260878967735002,"uuid":"189bd505-65f9-4c56-8f8a-11c92c711f73"}